  "summary": "I wrote the portal scene in `src/main.ts`, but I couldn't check it against the engine. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty in this sandbox, so `typecheck` reports `TS2307: Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'`, and `vite build` would fail here too. That is the only error. Every engine call was written from `llms.txt` and the docs recipes and never type-checked. Nothing has been run or seen in a browser.\n\nWhat the file builds:\n- **Portal:** a 20-block weathered-stone ring with glowing cyan runes on both faces, standing on a two-tier stone platform with a violet rune circle. A seven-pillar ruin (some capped, some broken) surrounds it, with fallen drums and about 60 rubble blocks.\n- **Vortex disc:** a custom GLSL shader draws logarithmic spiral arms in cyan and violet over a rotating noise field. It has a bright white-cyan core, centre ripples and a glowing rim. A second additive halo disc adds glow around the ring.\n- **Lighting:**\n  - A warm low dusk directional light with shadows, a cool fill, and a purple hemisphere light.\n  - Three point lights (cyan in front, violet behind, violet low) pulse with a period of about 5.7 s.\n  - The shader's `pls` uniform pulses on the same cycle.\n  - Haze comes from exponential fog, plus bloom and a vignette.\n- **Particles:** these are my own simulation, using instanced emissive spheres.\n  - 260 spiral sparks (130 cyan, 130 violet) curl inward and shrink into the portal, then respawn.\n  - Up to 90 pooled motes spawn on the platform at about 14 per second, rise with sway, and shrink to nothing.\n  - Dead mote slots are parked at a hidden transform.\n  - The sparks use size shrink for fading, because emissive colour isn't tinted by instance colour.\n- **Camera and state:** `camera.orbit` with a slow `autoRotate` of 0.08 rad/s. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\nUntested guesses about the engine:\n- That `setInstances` accepts a transforms array without colours.\n- That `blending: \"addit",
